This product includes software developed by OpenAI:
OpenAI Codex
https://github.com/openai/codex, commit ac54a05
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see third_party/codex/LICENSE
and third_party/codex/NOTICE).

third_party/codex holds Codex's own files, unmodified: LICENSE, NOTICE, its
goal extension (codex-rs/ext/goal: source, prompt templates and tests), and
the two files that extension's prompts depend on
(codex-rs/prompts/src/update_plan_instructions.rs and
codex-rs/core/src/context/user_goal.rs). The rest of Codex is left out.
Guardian's goal loop sends Codex's continuation and objective-updated prompts
word for word, and its get_goal and update_goal tools carry Codex's names,
descriptions and statuses. Codex's Rust code is not run by Guardian today. It
could be in part: its goal crate builds and passes its 36 tests unmodified, and
its goal store (codex-state) runs in a standalone 21 MB binary; only its
continuation scheduling starts Codex's own turns, which Cursor's stop hook has
to do instead. scripts/gen-vendored.mjs reads the text out of these files
into packages/core/src/goal/vendored.generated.ts.

This product includes software developed by DeepSeek:
DeepSeek Harness
https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness, commit fcc0ad4
Licensed under the MIT License (see third_party/deepseek-harness/LICENSE).

third_party/deepseek-harness holds DeepSeek Harness's own files, unmodified:
LICENSE, its goal packages (packages/goal: goal, goal-round-driver, tool-goal
and command-goal, with their tests and documentation) and
docs/subsystems/goal.md. The rest of the harness is left out. Guardian runs
two of its functions as they are, with types stripped: renderGoalRoundPrompt
(the <goal_round> prompt) and renderWrapupContext (the closing instructions),
and uses its blocked-round threshold and refusal message.

Guardian's goal state is kept by DeepSeek Harness's published packages
(@deepseek-ai/dsh-goal, dsh-session, dsh-session-projection, dsh-agent and
dsh-llm 0.2.2-rc.1, the vendored version, and @deepseek-ai/cordis 4.1.0, MIT),
bundled unmodified except that dsh-llm's run-time read of its own version is
inlined at build time (scripts/dsh-bundle.mjs). Every change to the goal is
made by its GoalService and read by its foldGoal; Guardian's adapter is
packages/core/src/goal/engine.ts. Its round driver and tool plumbing are not
run yet.

This product includes software developed by Google LLC:
Agent Development Kit (ADK) for Python
https://github.com/google/adk-python, commit c0bcdaa
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see
third_party/adk-python/LICENSE).

third_party/adk-python holds ADK's own files, unmodified, at their upstream
paths: LICENSE, README.md and the 115 files under src/google/adk that its
RubricBasedMultiTurnTrajectoryEvaluator loads. third_party/adk-python/
VENDORED.md, which is Guardian's, says what is left out. Guardian runs that
evaluator as it is, with ADK's judge prompt, sampling and aggregation, as the
second check when the agent reports the goal complete; its adapter is
packages/evaluator. The rubrics are the user's own "done when" items, plus one
sentence of Guardian's about unrequested work. ADK's dependencies (pydantic,
google-genai and 15 others, pinned in packages/evaluator/requirements.txt, each
under its own licence) are installed as wheels when the extension is packaged
and are not copied here. ADK's evaluators that call Vertex AI's hosted
evaluation are not used.

Codex's own goal store (the codex-state crate at ac54a05, Apache-2.0) runs
unmodified beside DeepSeek Harness's service: it is fetched from Codex's
repository at build time and linked into packages/codex-goals, and none of it
is copied here. It is told every change to the goal and keeps Codex's usage
accounting and token budget. Not run yet from Codex: its tool handlers and its
continuation scheduling. Not run yet from DeepSeek Harness: its tools, its
round driver and its /goal command.

This product includes Anthropic's Ralph Loop plugin
(https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official, commit 43fd1f9,
Apache-2.0), vendored unmodified in
third_party/claude-plugins-official/plugins/ralph-loop. Guardian runs its setup
